WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.643
In tutorial 5.8, you'll write
the pages Alaventra suggests,

00:00:10.693 --> 00:00:13.036
and see every check that runs on its own.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:19.207
First, scroll to Always on. This card
shows how many pages a week you get,

00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:21.293
and which keywords share them, in order.

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:27.562
Click Change to set your pages a week,
from none, which turns weekly pages off,

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:30.574
to three. Choose one, and click Save.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:35.082
Next, Suggestions lists
chances found in your own data,

00:00:35.132 --> 00:00:37.707
like these searches close to page one.

00:00:37.757 --> 00:00:41.939
A page losing visitors or a
rising search shows up here too.

00:00:42.902 --> 00:00:47.687
Each one says why, which page it improves,
and about how many credits it uses.

00:00:49.898 --> 00:00:55.473
Questions AI answers without you show up
too, as an AI answer page or an AI refresh,

00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:56.458
in Coming up.

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:01.748
Then click Write it on the ones
you want. The window shows why,

00:01:01.798 --> 00:01:04.742
what kind of page it is,
and the page it improves.

00:01:06.898 --> 00:01:09.298
Click Write it, with the
credits on the button,

00:01:09.348 --> 00:01:11.794
and the page arrives as its own report.

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:17.273
Now look at Monitoring. These
checks run on their own:

00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:22.180
your AI visibility and AI growth in
your weekly run, and a daily AI pulse.

00:01:23.423 --> 00:01:26.493
Then link building, your
backlinks, rank tracking,

00:01:26.543 --> 00:01:29.918
the weekly site report and
a monthly technical audit.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.813
Each shows when it runs next.

00:01:32.902 --> 00:01:36.427
Each card also has Last
report, and some have Run now.

00:01:36.477 --> 00:01:38.967
Settings turns each check on or off.

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:43.964
Finally, Next four weeks shows
every run on your calendar,

00:01:44.014 --> 00:01:47.447
and Recent automatic runs lists
what was delivered on its own.

00:01:49.448 --> 00:01:52.723
Now you know what runs on
its own, what waits for you,

00:01:52.773 --> 00:01:55.382
and which suggestions are
worth a page this week.

00:01:56.969 --> 00:02:01.574
So: set your weekly pages, read the
suggestions, write the ones you want,

00:02:01.624 --> 00:02:04.245
see the checks, and look
at the next four weeks.

00:02:05.423 --> 00:02:10.198
Your Pipeline runs on its own. Next,
see every page from written to live,

00:02:10.248 --> 00:02:12.171
in tutorial 6.1.
